From d1b6f19a89a9b2f5211a0f3cd38141016beb9a9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:27:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] Auto on a Mali GPU picks the software driver, and
 nothing else

Requirement, and the reason it is not already satisfied: on this device "no driver selected" is not a
neutral state. The runtime's built-in ICD is PanVK, so an Auto that selects nothing selects the GPU.
DriverPairs.recommendedKey already returns null for Family.MALI - verified, not assumed - so Auto
installs no Turnip pair here; what it did then was stop with "no drivers to set", leaving the
selection empty, which on a Mali device means the hardware driver.

Now the empty case looks for an imported software driver and selects it, saying which in the status
line, and with nothing imported it says what to import instead of quietly pointing the session at
Mali. Every line of this is behind DeviceSupport.mali(): an Adreno device never enters the function.

Also labels an imported software driver "software, no GPU" in the list. It needs a label because the
importer renames every driver to the same soname on disk - a lavapipe file is called
libvulkan_freedreno.so in the app's directory - so the file names cannot tell a driver that can fault
this GPU from one that cannot.

Checked: no recursion (setMode -> ensureAuto -> refreshDrivers; refreshDrivers assigns mode directly
and does not call back), both strings files parse and carry the new keys in en and es. Not checked:
compilation (no JDK here); CI does that. Two failed patch attempts before this one, both from anchors
I wrote from memory of the file instead of from the file - the second one is why every edit in this
commit is followed by a grep for what it was supposed to have added.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
